ivtc_cuda: add hardware inverse-telecine (field matching) through CUDA

New filter `ivtc_cuda`, the CUDA counterpart of ivtc_opencl for the zero-copy
NVDEC -> CUDA -> NVENC chain:

  -hwaccel cuda -hwaccel_output_format cuda ... -vf ivtc_cuda -c:v h264_nvenc

It is a second backend of the shared ivtc core (ivtc_common.c / ivtc.h): the
compare_fields decision, 5-frame decimation (vf_decimate maxbdiff/totdiff),
soft-pulldown (RFF) expansion and contiguous 23.976 emit timing are identical
to ivtc_opencl. vf_ivtc_cuda.cu ports the live OpenCL kernels (fm_absdiff,
fm_diffmap, fm_compare_accum, ivtc_diff) to pitched uchar/ushort luma with
16x16 block reductions; raw samples are scaled to the same units the OpenCL
UNORM reads give (0..255 for fieldmatch, 0..1 for decimation), so all
thresholds carry over. Field-match synthesis needs no kernel: the chosen
fields are woven with pitched cuMemcpy2DAsync copies, which is bit-depth and
chroma-layout agnostic. All work runs on the device stream with one sync per
frame (match accumulators) and one per cycle (decimation diffs); the output
comes from the filter's own CUDA pool so it feeds NVENC directly.

Supported sw_formats: nv12, yuv420p, p010, p016, yuv444p, yuv444p16.

compat/cuda/cuda_runtime.h (the clang/cuda-llvm shim) gains __shared__, which
no in-tree kernel needed before (__syncthreads is a clang builtin).

Credit: the field-matching algorithm and kernels are ported from QSVEnc
(QSVPipeline/rgy_filter_ivtc) by rigaya, used under the MIT License
(QSVEnc/NVEnc/VCEEnc, Copyright (c) 2014-2016 rigaya,
https://github.com/rigaya/QSVEnc). The CUDA filter scaffolding follows
FFmpeg's vf_bwdif_cuda.c.

Files: libavfilter/vf_ivtc_cuda.c, libavfilter/vf_ivtc_cuda.cu (new),
libavfilter/allfilters.c, libavfilter/Makefile, configure,
compat/cuda/cuda_runtime.h.

